COVID-19: On 26 March 2020, the Palestinian Authority released the National COVID-19 Response Plan to:
– present the Government’s strategy and actions;
– propose an aid coordination approach;
– identify critical support needs, including for the public health response to COVID-19, budget support to maintain government services, and diplomatic engagement with regional partners;
– describe the expectations of the longer-term economic impact of COVID-19 and required economic recovery actions.

The plan specifies a requirement of USD 120 million over 90 days for containment measures in a number of key sectors, including health, economy and social protection.

