The comprehensive program for the development of biotechnology in the Russian Federation for the period until 2020 (hereinafter referred to as the Program) was developed in accordance with the decision of the Government Commission on High Technologies and Innovations of April 1, 2011.

The goal of the Program is to achieve Russia's leading position in the field of biotechnology, including in certain areas of biomedicine, agrobiotechnology, industrial biotechnology and bioenergy, and to create a globally competitive sector of bioeconomics, which, along with nanoindustry and information technology, should become the basis for modernization and building a post-industrial economy.

The program is supposed to be implemented in two stages: Stage I - 2012 - 2015, Stage II - 2016 - 2020.

By 2015, it is planned to develop domestic demand and export of biotechnological products; creation of a production and technological base for the formation of new sub-sectors of industry, capable in the long term of replacing a substantial part of the products produced by the chemical synthesis method with biological synthesis products; creation of a technological and experimental-industrial base for the formation of a biofuel industry.

By 2020, it is planned to create institutional conditions for deep modernization of the technological base of the relevant industries through the mass introduction of biotechnology methods and products into production; integration of the scientific and technological sector of Russia into the international system of knowledge production with access to the accelerated development of scientific potential focused on the creation of knowledge and technologies capable, along with nanotechnologies and information technologies, of ensuring the modernization of the industrial sector.

The main objectives of the program:

creation of infrastructure for the development of biotechnology in Russia;
the formation and implementation of priority innovative and investment projects in biotechnology;
large-scale deployment of bio-industry in the regions of Russia across all sectors of biotechnology;
supporting the development of life sciences and physico-chemical biology;
the creation of modern educational programs and training systems in the field of biotechnology;
preservation and development of Russia's bio-resource potential as the basis of bio-industry;
the solution of relevant socio-economic, energy, environmental and other problems of the country by methods and means of biotechnology;
integration of domestic biotechnology into the global bioeconomy;
improving the legal, economic, informational and organizational basis for the development of biotechnology.

Expected results of the Program:

an increase of 8.3 times the volume of consumption of biotechnological products in Russia;
an increase in the volume of production of biotechnological products in Russia by 33 times;
50% reduction in the share of imports in the consumption of biotechnological products;
increase in the share of exports in the production of biotechnological products by more than 25 times;
reaching a level of biotechnological production in the amount of about 1% of GDP by 2020 and creating conditions for the sector to achieve at least 3% of GDP by 2030.
The implementation of the program will lead to significant social effects. In the field of medical care, due to the widespread adoption of new diagnostic methods and the practice of personalized medicine, the effectiveness of treatment will sharply increase. In the field of ecology, effective methods for eliminating pollution and preventing harmful anthropogenic impacts on the environment will be created. The introduction of biotechnology in agriculture will contribute to improving the food security of the country. The development of bioenergy will contribute to the emergence of new available energy sources.

The document was developed by the Ministry of Regional Development of the Russian Federation in pursuance of subparagraph “a” of paragraph 2 of Decree of the President of the Russian Federation dated December 19, 2012 No. 1666 “On the Strategy of the State National Policy of the Russian Federation for the period until 2025” .

The purpose of the development and adoption of the plan is to coordinate the actions of federal executive bodies, executive bodies of the constituent entities of the Russian Federation, local authorities, civil society institutions in the implementation of the state national policy of the Russian Federation.

The action plan consists of 82 paragraphs providing for activities that correspond to the priority areas of the state national policy of the Russian Federation, aimed at:

- improving public administration in the field of state national policy of the Russian Federation;

- ensuring the equal rights of citizens, the implementation of their constitutional rights in the field of state national policy of the Russian Federation;

- Strengthening the unity and spiritual community of the multinational people of the Russian Federation (Russian nation);

- ensuring interethnic peace and harmony, harmonization of interethnic (interethnic) relations;

- ensuring socio-economic conditions for the effective implementation of state national policy of the Russian Federation;

- promoting the preservation and development of the ethnocultural diversity of the peoples of Russia;

- development of the educational system, civil patriotic education of the younger generations;

- support for the Russian language as the state language of the Russian Federation and the languages ​​of the peoples of Russia;

- creating conditions for social and cultural adaptation and integration of migrants;

- Information Support;

- improving the interaction of state authorities and local self-government with civil society institutions;

- the international cooperation.

The implementation of the action plan will contribute to the harmonization of inter-ethnic relations, the development of the linguistic and ethnocultural diversity of the Russian Federation, the popularization of the history and cultures of the peoples of Russia, the prevention and early warning of conflicts in the field of inter-ethnic relations.

The action plan is a mechanism for implementing the Strategy of the state national policy of the Russian Federation for the period until 2025.

The government approved the Concept of sustainable development of the indigenous peoples of the North, Siberia and the Far East of the Russian Federation (hereinafter - the Concept).

The purpose of the Concept is to create conditions for the sustainable development of indigenous peoples of the North by strengthening their socio-economic potential while preserving the original habitat, traditional lifestyle and cultural values ​​of these peoples.

The concept provides:

preservation of the original habitat and traditional nature management to ensure and develop the traditional way of life of the indigenous peoples of the North;
development and modernization of traditional economic activity;
improving the quality of life of the indigenous peoples of the North to the average Russian level;
creating conditions for improving demographic indicators, including by reducing child mortality and increasing life expectancy to the average Russian level;
increasing access to educational services, taking into account ethnocultural characteristics;
assistance to the development of communities and other forms of self-government of the indigenous peoples of the North;
preservation of cultural heritage.

The concept is planned to be implemented in three stages: the first stage is 2009–2011, the second stage is 2012–2015, and the third stage is 2016–2025.

The purpose of the Program is to ensure stable growth in agricultural production obtained through the use of seeds of new domestic varieties and breeding products, technologies for the production of high-quality feed, feed additives for animals and medicines for veterinary use, pesticides and agrochemicals of biological origin, processing and storage of agricultural products, raw materials and food, modern diagnostic tools, methods of quality control of agricultural products and raw food and examination of the genetic material.

The state coordinator of the Program is the Ministry of Agriculture of Russia, the responsible executors of the Program are the Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Russia.

The program, in particular, provides for:

- creating conditions for the development of scientific, technical activities and obtaining the results necessary for the creation of technologies, products, goods and services that ensure the independence and competitiveness of the domestic agricultural sector;

- Attracting investment in the agricultural sector;

- the creation and implementation of technologies for the production of seeds of the highest categories (original and elite) of agricultural plants, pedigree products (material) in the areas of domestic crop production and animal husbandry, which currently have a high degree of dependence on seeds or pedigree products (material) of foreign production;

- improvement of the training system and additional professional education for the agricultural sector, focused on quick adaptation to the requirements of scientific and technological progress.

Implementation of the Program will be financed from the federal budget (26.1 billion rubles) under the State Program for the Development of Agriculture and Regulation of Agricultural Products, Raw Materials and Food Markets for 2013–2020, state programs “Development of Science and Technology” for 2013–2020 years, “Development of education” for 2013–2020, “Development of industry and increasing its competitiveness”, “Information society (2011–2020”)). Financing is also provided for from the budgets of the constituent entities of the Federation and extrabudgetary sources (25 billion rubles).

The effectiveness of the Program will be evaluated on the basis of the system of target indicators and indicators of the Program. Target indicators, in particular, include increasing innovative activity in agriculture, attracting investment in agriculture, increasing the level of provision of infrastructure to the agro-industrial complex.

The state policy on managing the land fund of Russia is aimed at creating and improving legal, economic, social and organizational conditions for the development of land relations.

The signed order approved the Fundamentals of the state policy on the use of the land fund in the Russian Federation for 2012-2017 (hereinafter - the Fundamentals).

The objectives of the Fundamentals are to increase the efficiency of use and protect land as the main component of the environment and the main means of production in agriculture while ensuring the food security of the country.

The main objectives of the state policy on land management:

- creating conditions for organizing the rational and efficient use of land, which includes taking into account social and industry needs, the requirements for sustainable development of territories, as well as compliance with guarantees of the rights of participants in land relations;

- ensuring the protection of nature and the environment, including the protection of land and the preservation of cultural heritage;

- preservation and improvement of the quality of land;

- maintaining the status of protected natural territories as protected lands as part of the land fund;

- providing conditions for increasing the efficiency of civil turnover of land, including those aimed at protecting rights to real estate, as well as to reduce administrative barriers and ensure taxation of real estate.

The fundamentals, in particular, provide for the improvement of the procedure for determining the legal regime of land plots by excluding from the land legislation the principle of dividing land for the intended purpose into categories; providing guarantees of land rights and protecting the rights and legitimate interests of owners, land users, landowners and tenants of land plots; improvement of state land supervision and municipal land control; development of state land monitoring.

The government approved the Concept for the development of a system of specially protected natural territories of federal significance for the period until 2020 (hereinafter referred to as the Concept, specially protected natural territories) and a plan for its implementation.

The Concept was developed in accordance with the Environmental Doctrine of the Russian Federation (approved by Government Decree of August 31, 2002 No. 1225-r), the Concept of Long-Term Social and Economic Development until 2020 (approved by Government Decree of November 17, 2008 No. 1662-r), the Main Areas activities of the Government until 2012 (approved by order of the Government of November 17, 2008 No. 1663-r).

The concept defines the main directions of development of the system of specially protected natural territories and measures to increase the effectiveness of public administration in this area.

Specially protected natural territories, fully or partially withdrawn from economic use, are of exceptional importance for the conservation of biological and landscape diversity as the basis of the biosphere. Given the increasing threat of natural disasters and changes in the environment as a result of economic activity, the main purpose of specially protected natural areas is to provide the services demanded by society in the field of:

- maintaining the environmental stability of territories significantly altered by economic activity;

- reproduction in natural conditions of valuable renewable natural resources;

- maintaining a healthy environment for people's lives and creating conditions for the development of regulated tourism and recreation;

- implementation of environmental education programs;

- fundamental and applied research in the field of natural sciences.

About 12 thousand specially protected natural territories of various levels and categories have been created in Russia.

The basis of the system of specially protected natural territories is 102 state nature reserves (hereinafter - reserves), 42 national parks and 70 state nature reserves of federal significance (hereinafter - federal reserves).

The purpose of the Concept is to develop a system of specially protected natural territories by increasing the effectiveness of public administration in the organization and functioning of a system of specially protected natural territories in the interests of sustainable development of the country, ensuring environmental safety, protecting biological and landscape diversity, preserving and rational use of natural and cultural heritage.

The concept provides for the solution of the following main tasks:

- Formation of a representative geographic network of specially protected natural areas, primarily the creation of new reserves and national parks;

- providing an effective system for the protection of natural and historical-cultural complexes and objects in specially protected natural territories;

- The development of environmental education activities of nature reserves and national parks throughout the country;

- involvement of specially protected natural territories in the development of ecological tourism;

- ensuring the relevance of the scientific products of nature reserves and national parks and the results of their environmental monitoring;

- Integration of specially protected natural territories into the sphere of socio-economic development of regions;

- enhancing the role of specially protected natural territories in the formation of a positive international image of Russia.

The concept will be implemented taking into account the priority of conservation of natural and historical-cultural complexes and objects over other tasks of specially protected natural areas; scientific validity of managerial decision making; socio-economic aspects when making management decisions; systematic and integrated solution of problems in the field of organization and functioning of specially protected natural territories; openness and accessibility of information in this area.

The Concept provides an assessment of the current demographic situation in the Russian Federation and its development trends, defines the principles of the demographic policy of the Russian Federation (the basis of which is the complexity of solving demographic problems, the choice of the most problematic issues in each direction of demographic development, taking into account regional characteristics of demographic development, coordination of legislative and executive bodies of state power at the federal, regional and municipal levels x), as well as the main tasks of the demographic policy of the Russian Federation.

The main objectives of the Concept:

- reduction in the mortality rate of citizens, primarily of working age;

- reduction of maternal and infant mortality, strengthening the reproductive health of the population, the health of children and adolescents;

- maintaining and strengthening the health of the population, increasing the duration of active life, creating conditions and creating motivation for maintaining a healthy lifestyle, significantly reducing the incidence of socially significant and dangerous diseases, and improving the quality of life of patients suffering from chronic diseases and persons with disabilities;

- increase the birth rate;

- Strengthening the institution of the family, the revival and preservation of the spiritual and moral traditions of family relations;

- regulation of internal and external migration, attracting migrants in accordance with the needs of demographic and socio-economic development, taking into account the need for their social adaptation and integration.

The concept also identified comprehensive measures implemented in three stages, the result of which should be an improvement in the demographic situation in the country.

Such measures, in particular, include: the formation of motivation for a healthy lifestyle in various groups of the population, especially in the younger generation; carrying out preventive measures for the early detection of health disorders; early diagnosis of diseases using advanced technologies; increasing the availability and quality of free medical care; improving the material and technical and staffing of health facilities; application of new innovative treatment technologies and the development of high-tech medical care; introduction of comprehensive health and rehabilitation programs; propaganda of family values, strengthening state support for families with children; creating conditions for the integration of immigrants in Russian society.

