The Strategy is an interdisciplinary document of strategic planning in the field of development of small and medium enterprises. It is the basis for the development and updating of state programs of the Russian Federation, state programs of constituent entities of the Federation, municipal programs, as well as planned and program-targeted documents aimed at the development of small and medium-sized enterprises.

The purpose of the Strategy is to develop the sphere of small and medium-sized enterprises as one of the factors of innovative development of the country and improve the sectoral structure of the economy. The strategy is aimed at creating a competitive, flexible and adaptive economy that provides a high level of individualization of goods and services, high speed of technological renewal and stable employment.

Priority areas of the Strategy:

- integration of support functions for small and medium enterprises;

- stimulating demand for the products of small and medium-sized enterprises, including through expanding access of such enterprises to the procurement of goods, work, services by organizations of the public sector of the economy;

- creating conditions for increasing labor productivity in small and medium enterprises;

- ensuring the availability of financial resources for small and medium enterprises;

- improvement of taxation and non-tax payments policies;

- improving the quality of state regulation in the field of small and medium-sized enterprises;

- stimulating the development of entrepreneurial activity in certain territories.

The implementation of the Strategy by 2030 will make it possible to double the share of small and medium enterprises in gross domestic product (from 20 to 40%), the turnover of small and medium enterprises - 2.5 times, labor productivity in this sector - two times, the share manufacturing industry in the turnover of the sector of small and medium-sized enterprises (excluding individual entrepreneurs) - up to 20% and the share of the number of people employed in this area in the total number of employed people - up to 35%.

The decision is aimed at ensuring coordination of actions of authorities at all levels, representatives of the business community and organizations that form the support infrastructure in the field of development of small and medium-sized enterprises.

