The Strategy for sustainable development of rural territories of the Russian Federation for the period until 2030 was prepared by the Ministry of Agriculture in pursuance of an order from the President of Russia following a meeting of the State Council and the Council on the implementation of priority national projects and demographic policies on April 21, 2014 ( No. Pr-995GS of May 1, 2014, subparagraph “a” of paragraph 1 ).

The signed decree approves the Strategy for Sustainable Development of Rural Territories of the Russian Federation for the period up to 2030 (hereinafter - the Strategy).

The strategy was developed in accordance with the Federal Law “On Strategic Planning in the Russian Federation” .

Strategy Objectives:

- Creation of favorable socio-economic conditions for rural areas to fulfill their socially significant functions and to solve the tasks of territorial development;

- ensuring stabilization of the rural population and creating conditions for its growth by reducing mortality, increasing life expectancy, reducing the migration outflow of the population;

- providing employment, improving the level and quality of life of the rural population, taking into account modern requirements and standards;

- improving the efficiency of agriculture and the contribution of rural territories to the socio-economic development of the country.

The strategy provides for two stages of its implementation: the transitional stage (2015–2020), the main stage (2021–2030).

Priorities of the transitional stage of the Strategy implementation: the formation of mechanisms and incentives for stabilizing the demographic situation, ensuring the development of housing, engineering and road transport infrastructure, adjusting existing imbalances in ensuring the accessibility and quality of education and health services, ensuring epizootic well-being, developing and implementing a system of social standards, improvement of legal regulation to solve the identified problems of sustainable development of rural areas s, the formation of effective mechanisms for inter-agency cooperation and coordination to achieve sustainable rural development at the federal, regional and local levels.

At the main stage, the development of rural infrastructure will continue along with the intensification of activities to improve the quality of life of rural residents. The priorities of this stage are the formation and implementation of a balanced system of mechanisms and incentives to improve the demographic situation, taking into account regional specifics, promoting the introduction of new cost-effective mechanisms of economic activity and the provision of social services, accelerated development of communications and communications infrastructure, comprehensive provision of cultural and leisure needs of the population.

The main mechanisms for implementing the Strategy are the state programs of the Russian Federation and state programs of the constituent entities of the Federation.

Achieving the goals and objectives of the Strategy is determined by the achievement by 2030 of the main targets, including:

- stabilization of the rural population at the level of 35 million people;

- increase the expected life expectancy of the rural population to 75.6 years;

- reducing the migration outflow of the rural population to 74.1 thousand people;

- ensuring the average annual growth rate of agricultural production in the amount of 5.5%;

- increase the level of employment of the rural population to 65.5%;

- expanding the network of feldsher-midwife centers and (or) offices of general practitioners in rural areas by 1.7 thousand units;

- increase the share of the rural population, systematically engaged in physical education and sports, up to 37.3%;

- increase in the proportion of rural settlements that have a connection on paved roads with a network of roads, up to 80%.

The Strategy was developed taking into account the National Security Strategy of Russia (approved by Decree of the President of Russia dated December 31, 2015 No. 683), the Fundamentals of state policy in the field of ensuring chemical and biological safety of Russia for the period up to 2025 and the future perspective (approved by the President of Russia on November 1, 2013 No. Pr-2573), of the Global Plan of Action to Combat Antimicrobial Resistance, adopted at the 68th World Health Assembly in May 2015.

The purpose of the Strategy is to prevent and limit the spread of antimicrobial resistance in Russia.

The strategy defines the state policy to prevent and limit the spread of the resistance of microorganisms to antimicrobials, chemical and biological agents.

The strategy, in particular, provides for:

- study of the mechanisms of occurrence of antimicrobial resistance and systematic monitoring of its spread;

- improvement of measures to prevent and limit the spread and circulation of pathogens with antimicrobial resistance;

- the development of antimicrobial agents and alternative methods, technologies and means of prevention, diagnosis and treatment of infectious diseases of humans, animals and plants;

- informing the public about the use of antimicrobials and the problems of antimicrobial resistance;

- ensuring interagency cooperation and the development of international cooperation in the field of prevention and limitation of antimicrobial resistance.

The strategy is planned to be implemented in two stages.

At the first stage (until 2020), it is envisaged to increase public awareness of the rational use of antimicrobial drugs, their adequate replacement, the inadmissibility of self-medication, an increase in the coverage of immunization prophylaxis and a healthy lifestyle; increase the detectability of resistance to antimicrobials, chemical and biological agents of the forms of pathogens of infectious diseases of people, animals and plants, the establishment of basic indicators characterizing the prevalence of antimicrobial resistance.

At the second stage (until 2030), it is planned to reduce the number of cases associated with the provision of medical care, infectious diseases that are caused by microorganisms with multidrug resistance.

The implementation of the Strategy will increase the effectiveness of the prevention and treatment of infectious and parasitic diseases of people, animals and plants, and reduce the severity and duration of treatment of diseases.

The government approved the Concept of sustainable development of the indigenous peoples of the North, Siberia and the Far East of the Russian Federation (hereinafter - the Concept).

The purpose of the Concept is to create conditions for the sustainable development of indigenous peoples of the North by strengthening their socio-economic potential while preserving the original habitat, traditional lifestyle and cultural values ​​of these peoples.

The concept provides:

preservation of the original habitat and traditional nature management to ensure and develop the traditional way of life of the indigenous peoples of the North;
development and modernization of traditional economic activity;
improving the quality of life of the indigenous peoples of the North to the average Russian level;
creating conditions for improving demographic indicators, including by reducing child mortality and increasing life expectancy to the average Russian level;
increasing access to educational services, taking into account ethnocultural characteristics;
assistance to the development of communities and other forms of self-government of the indigenous peoples of the North;
preservation of cultural heritage.

The concept is planned to be implemented in three stages: the first stage is 2009–2011, the second stage is 2012–2015, and the third stage is 2016–2025.

The Government has implemented other programs and overhead expenses of the Ministry of Agriculture. The Government has allocated 40.13 billion rubles (US$660.000.000) for the following:
- Sustainable Development of Rural Territories in 2014-2017 and until 2020;
- Development of irrigation;
- Support of pre-school, school, higher and professional education
- Other programs and expenses.

COVID-19: After consulting with the business community, the Russian Ministry of Economic Development has determined the sectors, which are the most affected by the current economic situation concerning COVID-19. The companies in the listed sectors will benefit from a number of support measures, including in the area of tax and customs.

The list published on the Ministry’s official website includes, in particular, the following sectors:

- transport;

- culture and entertainment;

- sports;

- travel and tourism;

- food services;

- further education;

- organisation of conferences and exhibitions;

- provision of household services.

According to the instructions of the President of Russia Vladimir Putin, the following assistance will be provided to these industries:

- six-month payment deferrals for all taxes (excluding VAT) for SMEs; 
- six-month payment deferrals for insurance premiums to state extra-budgetary funds for microenterprises;
- six-month payment deferrals for loans for small and medium-sized enterprises;
- additional measures to ensure sustainable lending to the real estate sector, including the provision of state guarantees and subsidies;
- a six-month moratorium for insolvency claims and claims for debt collection;
- deferral for small and medium-sized businesses to make rental payments for federal property;
- expanding the ability of SMEs to obtain loans at a reduced rate of not more than 8.5 percent;
- moratorium on test purchases, scheduled and unscheduled inspections;
- reduction of social contribution rates for SMEs. The cumulative social contribution rate for SMEs is to be reduced from 30 percent to 15 percent for salaries exceeding the minimum monthly wage.

The Plan for the implementation in 2015-2017 of the second stage of the National Strategy for Children was prepared pursuant to Decree of the President of Russia dated June 1, 2012 No. 761 "On the National Strategy of Actions for Children for 2012-2017" (hereinafter - the National Strategy) and instructions of the President following a meeting of the State Council Presidium on state policy in the field of family, motherhood and childhood on March 4, 2014 ( No. Pr-411GS, subparagraph "b" of paragraph 1 ).

By order of the Government of October 15, 2012 No. 1916-r , a plan of priority measures for the implementation of the first stage of the National Strategy was approved.

In accordance with this plan approved:

- The concept of state family policy in the Russian Federation for the period until 2025 ;

- The concept of developing, until 2017, a network of mediation services in order to implement restorative justice in relation to children, including those who have committed socially dangerous acts, but have not reached the age at which criminal liability arises in the Russian Federation ;

- Strategy for the development of the children's goods industry for the period until 2020 ;

- A set of measures aimed at ensuring guaranteed access to income and social services for families with children, including low-income people, for the period until 2016;

- The concept of development of additional education of children .

The signed decree approved the action plan for 2015-2017 to implement the most important provisions of the National Strategy (hereinafter - the plan), that is, its second stage.

The plan contains 81 events and was prepared taking into account the results of the analysis of the situation in the field of protecting the rights of children in Russia, including the results of monitoring enforcement in this area.

The plan provides for measures to improve legislation in the field of family policy, reduce poverty among families with children, create a safe and comfortable family environment for children, prevent the removal of a child from the family, ensure accessibility and quality of education, search and support talented children and youth, and develop an additional system education, ensuring information security of childhood, the formation of a modern model of organizing recreation and health of children, expanding the participation of children in social life and the adoption of decisions affecting their interests, the prevention of violence against minors and the rehabilitation of children who are victims of violence.

The action plan will be implemented in conjunction with other strategic documents that determine the priority areas of state policy in relation to childhood. This includes the Concept of socio-economic development of the Russian Federation for the period up to 2020 , the Concept of demographic policy of the Russian Federation for the period up to 2025 , priority national projects corresponding to state, federal target and departmental programs, as well as regional strategies (programs) of actions in against children.

The objectives of the Strategy are to ensure the quality of food products as an essential component of improving health, increasing the duration and quality of life of the population, promoting and stimulating the growth of demand and supply for higher-quality food products, and ensuring compliance with consumer rights to purchase quality products.

The achievement of these goals of the Strategy is planned to be achieved by implementing the following tasks:

improvement and development of the regulatory framework in the field of food product quality, including legal aspects related to effective compensation mechanisms for protecting consumer rights;
improvement and development of the methodological base for assessing the conformity of food product quality indicators;
ensuring monitoring of the quality of food products;
improvement of state regulation in the field of food product quality, including in terms of ensuring state control (supervision) and application of administrative measures for non-compliance by the manufacturer (contractor, seller, person acting as a foreign manufacturer) of food product quality requirements;
creating a unified food product traceability information system; development and implementation of a food product quality management system;
creation of mechanisms to stimulate producers to produce food products that meet the quality criteria and principles of healthy eating;
creation of conditions for the production of new-generation food products with specified quality characteristics;
revival of the production of food ingredients in the Russian Federation;
updating the current standards for the content of food additives, flavoring substances, biologically active substances, drug residues for veterinary use and plant protection products in food products;
priority development of scientific research in the field of nutrition, including the prevention of the most common noncommunicable diseases and the development of production technologies aimed at improving the quality of food products;
promoting healthy eating principles.

Expected Results

The implementation of the Strategy is designed to contribute to:

achieving mass commitment to the principles of healthy eating as one of the factors of a healthy lifestyle;
increase the share of quality food products in the structure of the food market, primarily domestic production;
reduction in the proportion of food products in circulation that can lead to the risk of its harmful effects on humans and future generations;
the creation of a holistic scientific system that provides on an ongoing basis comprehensive research in the field of production, circulation and consumption of quality food products, including those related to advanced technologies;
human resources development in the field of food production;
creating a favorable investment climate for the domestic business community in the field of food production, taking into account the growing needs of the population;
reducing the cost of providing medical care due to the need to treat diseases of the population associated with poor-quality, including malnutrition and malnutrition;
increased consumer confidence in domestic food products by increasing its competitiveness, improving consumer properties of products while maintaining its level of accessibility for the population.

The comprehensive program for the development of biotechnology in the Russian Federation for the period until 2020 (hereinafter referred to as the Program) was developed in accordance with the decision of the Government Commission on High Technologies and Innovations of April 1, 2011.

The goal of the Program is to achieve Russia's leading position in the field of biotechnology, including in certain areas of biomedicine, agrobiotechnology, industrial biotechnology and bioenergy, and to create a globally competitive sector of bioeconomics, which, along with nanoindustry and information technology, should become the basis for modernization and building a post-industrial economy.

The program is supposed to be implemented in two stages: Stage I - 2012 - 2015, Stage II - 2016 - 2020.

By 2015, it is planned to develop domestic demand and export of biotechnological products; creation of a production and technological base for the formation of new sub-sectors of industry, capable in the long term of replacing a substantial part of the products produced by the chemical synthesis method with biological synthesis products; creation of a technological and experimental-industrial base for the formation of a biofuel industry.

By 2020, it is planned to create institutional conditions for deep modernization of the technological base of the relevant industries through the mass introduction of biotechnology methods and products into production; integration of the scientific and technological sector of Russia into the international system of knowledge production with access to the accelerated development of scientific potential focused on the creation of knowledge and technologies capable, along with nanotechnologies and information technologies, of ensuring the modernization of the industrial sector.

The main objectives of the program:

creation of infrastructure for the development of biotechnology in Russia;
the formation and implementation of priority innovative and investment projects in biotechnology;
large-scale deployment of bio-industry in the regions of Russia across all sectors of biotechnology;
supporting the development of life sciences and physico-chemical biology;
the creation of modern educational programs and training systems in the field of biotechnology;
preservation and development of Russia's bio-resource potential as the basis of bio-industry;
the solution of relevant socio-economic, energy, environmental and other problems of the country by methods and means of biotechnology;
integration of domestic biotechnology into the global bioeconomy;
improving the legal, economic, informational and organizational basis for the development of biotechnology.

Expected results of the Program:

an increase of 8.3 times the volume of consumption of biotechnological products in Russia;
an increase in the volume of production of biotechnological products in Russia by 33 times;
50% reduction in the share of imports in the consumption of biotechnological products;
increase in the share of exports in the production of biotechnological products by more than 25 times;
reaching a level of biotechnological production in the amount of about 1% of GDP by 2020 and creating conditions for the sector to achieve at least 3% of GDP by 2030.
The implementation of the program will lead to significant social effects. In the field of medical care, due to the widespread adoption of new diagnostic methods and the practice of personalized medicine, the effectiveness of treatment will sharply increase. In the field of ecology, effective methods for eliminating pollution and preventing harmful anthropogenic impacts on the environment will be created. The introduction of biotechnology in agriculture will contribute to improving the food security of the country. The development of bioenergy will contribute to the emergence of new available energy sources.

