The National Standards and Quality Policy Implementation Plan (NSQPIP) provides interventions and activities to realize the objectives in order to achieve the desired outcomes. The Ministry of Trade, Industry and Cooperatives will take the lead in the implementation of the NSQPIP. A number of other Government Ministries, Departments and Agencies (MDAs), and the Private Sector indicated in the NSQPIP have their role to play as well. The NSQPIP fits well in the overall implementation of a number of other related policies as shown in this document.
The NSQPIP activities are clustered in seven broad groups of outcomes, namely:
1. A rationalized, harmonized and strong regulatory framework with regard to standards, metrology, accreditation and technical regulations;
2. A formal framework to enhance coordination and collaboration among regulatory authorities and national quality infrastructure institutions;
3. An improved national quality infrastructure with appropriate technical capacity;
4. A strong human resource capability in the national quality infrastructure;
5. An enhanced awareness and dialogue amongst all stakeholders regarding standards, technical regulations, metrology, accreditation and conformity assessment.
6. Support MSMEs to conform to national standards and comply with technical regulations; and
7. Support both the Public and Private Sector entities to conform to set standards.
Each of these seven broad groups of interventions has been provided with detailed activities, interventions and actions to facilitate the implementation of the national standards and quality policy. The interventions and actions have also been grouped into three phases, namely the initial Phase I (from September 2014 to June 2015), an intermediate Phase II (from July 2015 to December 2016) and the final Phase III (consisting of 2017 and 2019). After five years the policy document will be reviewed and a new implementation plan developed.

